# Production Suricata drop list — change-managed via git.
# Copy this file to /etc/suricata-drop.list on the agents:
#   cp etc/suricata-drop.list.production /etc/suricata-drop.list
# Re-applied every 6h by refresh-suricata-rules.sh (suricata-update regenerates
# the ruleset and would otherwise revert drops back to alerts).
#
# Entry types (one per line, '#' comments and blank lines ignored):
#   category:ET MALWARE    # flip every alert rule whose msg:"..." starts "ET MALWARE"
#   2034567                # flip a single rule by SID
#
# NOTE (verified on live ET Open free, 2026-09-11): there is NO "ET TROJAN"
# prefix in the free feed — Trojan signatures were consolidated into
# "ET MALWARE" (26k+ rules). Do not re-add it; it WARNs as unmatched.
#
# WARNING: `drop` rules in inline (NFQUEUE/IPS) mode BLOCK traffic outright.
# ET MALWARE / ET CNC are high-confidence C2/malware categories, but always
# `suricata -T` validate + watch alerts after any change here.
#
# Production set (Ko Ye, 2026-09-11):
category:ET MALWARE
category:ET CNC
2034567
